findings.description:
The success signal for the second oracle (lines 22, 38) is a findings count. The skill itself undermines that in three ways:

- **The count is prompt-anchored.** `commands/analysis/tech-debt-audit.md:68` instructs "Aim for 30–80 findings; padding past that is noise." A cleaner codebase will still yield about 30.
- **Repeat runs are not independent.** Repeat-run mode (`tech-debt-audit.md:103`) reads the previous audit file and marks RESOLVED/NEW. The "after" measurement is conditioned on the "before", and line 83's audit variance cannot be estimated from such runs.
- **The unit does not match the intervention.** The audit covers the whole repository, including code that predates the pipeline. The pre-emption prompt only affects newly dispatched code, so a whole-project count barely moves.

Line 85 covers attribution in general but none of these. The document also never requires recording whether pre-emption (and which version) was active on a run, so before/after cannot be partitioned.

The architecture should commit to:

- a metrology-mode audit with no count target and no prior-audit read;
- repeated baseline runs to set a noise floor before any delta is reported;
- a metric scoped to code produced after the intervention;
- a per-run intervention marker.
